# Grok Build first (tier 1)

OpenSesame Cloud Agents use a **three-tier coding chain** (see also
`.cursor/rules/kimi-first.mdc` for tier 2). **All implementation edits go
through tier 1 while Grok Build quota allows.** The Cursor agent orchestrates:
plan, review, test, provenance, and PRs — it does not hand-write product code
while tier 1 is available.

## Tier 1 — Grok Build CLI

1. Run `scripts/dev/agent-coding-preflight.sh` (or `scripts/dev/grok-preflight.sh`
   plus `scripts/dev/grok-resolve-model.sh`) before batch coding.
2. Resolve the model: `scripts/dev/grok-resolve-model.sh` prints the pin
   (`grok-4.7` minimum; use a newer id from `grok models` when listed).
3. Delegate coding:

   ```bash
   model="$(scripts/dev/grok-resolve-model.sh)"
   scripts/dev/grok-headless.sh -p "<task>" -m "$model" --always-approve --output-format json
   ```

4. **Auth:** prefer Cursor Runtime Secret `XAI_API_KEY`. A depleted key shadows
   device OIDC — run through `grok-headless.sh` when using `~/.grok/auth.json`.
   If Grok needs login, surface `grok login --device-code` (link + code) to the
   human immediately; do not block silently.

## When to leave tier 1 (tier 2 or 3)

Fall back only when `grok` exits non-zero and stderr/JSON indicates **weekly
limit**, **quota**, **usage exceeded**, **402**, **403 credits**, or **429**.
Then use **Kimi Code CLI (tier 2)** per `kimi-first.mdc`. When Kimi is also
exhausted, use **Cursor (tier 3)** — Grok 4.7 for security testing and
red-team work; Composer / auto for everything else.

Record the tier used and why in the PR **Provenance** section and
`docs/audit/2026-10-provenance.md` when material.
